From eabf90ba366b41c00d404735e3b1f49697e6e15e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "tianxu.zhang" <tianxu.zhang@bytedance.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:46:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: stream single DSML calls incrementally

Patch 0048 deliberately preserves the old one-call stream: when
parallel_tool_calls is false, it suppresses every tool delta and sends the
first parsed call only after generation ends. Coding agents commonly set
that policy, so their largest Write/Edit arguments still leave the client
silent until the full call is complete.

Pass the policy's one-call limit into the existing DSML streamer, cap it
before a second call header can escape, and settle the streamed first call
against the same max-one final parse. Keep legacy XML calls buffered under
the one-call policy. Parallel DSML streams, non-stream replies, and requests
without tools are unchanged.

Extend 0048's route test to verify that a two-call answer streams only its
first call, in multiple argument deltas, with bytes identical to the whole
reply.

